$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The palladium catalyzed cross-coupling reaction with aryl halide was
performed according to the literature procedure.2 Pd[P(t-Bu)3]2 (38.3 mg,
0.075 mmol) was placed in an oven-dried reaction vial under argon
atmosphere. Dry THF (1.5 mL) and bromobenzotrifluoride (371.3 mg, 1.65
mmol) were added to the vial at room temperature followed by addition of
a solution of (Z)-5a (648.7 mg, 1.5 mmol) in dry THF (3 mL). Then, a
solution of NaOH (180 mg, 4.5 mmol), H2O (324 mg, 18 mmol), in dry THF
(0.75 mL) was successively added. After stirring for 12 h at 60 ºC,
reaction mixture was quenched by H2O and extracted with CHCl3 three
times. The combined organic layer was then dried over MgSO4. The crude
material was purified by flush column chromatography (SiO2,
CH2Cl2/Hexane, 0:100-2:98). The corresponding coupling product (E)-12
(652.1 mg, 1.45 mmol, 96%) as a white solid. 1H NMR (392 MHz, CDCl3, δ):
0.46 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H), 0.71-0.82 (m, 4H), 1.17 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H),
1.75 (quin, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H), 2.26 (t, J = 6.7 Hz, 2H), 2.34 (t, J = 7.4
Hz, 2H), 7.30 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.38-7.46 (m, 6H), 7.59 (d, J = 7.6
Hz, 2H), 7.66-7.68 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (99 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 13.7 (CH3), 14.5
(CH2), 22.3 (CH2), 25.1 (CH2), 30.5 (CH2), 36.3 (CH2), 41.0 (CH2), 124.3
(C-F, q, J = 254.0 Hz, C), 125.0 (C-F, q, J = 3.5 Hz, CH), 127.9 (CH),
128.2 (CH), 129.1 (C-F, q, J = 30.3 Hz, C) 129.5 (CH), 135.1 (C), 135.4
(CH), 137.7 (C), 147.0 (C), 150.4 (C). HRMS-EI (m/z): [M]+ calcd for
C28H29F3Si, 450.19906; found, 450.19835.
