$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
4-Chloro-6-(3-pyridinyl)-3-quinolinecarboxamide (12) Cesium carbonate
(14.4 g, 44.2 mmol) was added to 3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-
dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyridine (3.74 g, 17.7 mmol),
6-bromo-4-chloroquinoline-3-carboxamide (5.1 g, 17.7 mmol) and
tetrakis(triphenylphoshine)palladium (1.0 g, 0.9 mmol) in dioxane (45 mL)
and water (6.4 mL) at 20 °C under nitrogen. The resulting slurry was
stirred at 100 °C for 5 hours and allowed to cool to RT. Water (150 mL)
was then added and the solid was filtered, washed with water (2 x 100 mL)
and MeCN (3 x 80 mL) and dried at 50 °C under vacuum.
4-Chloro-6-(1-methyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-3-quinolinecarboxamide (24) The
title compound was obtained (13.0 g, 96%) from
6-bromo-4-chloroquinoline-3- carboxamide (13.5 g, 47.3 mmol) and
1-methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole
(10.3 g, 49.7 mmol) following the same procedure as that described for
analogue 12. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6, 303 K) 3.92 (3H, s), 7.92 (1H, s),
8.10 (2H, d), 8.14-8.18 (2H, m), 8.35 (1H, d), 8.45 (1H, s), 8.78 (1H,s).
m/z 287.0 (M+H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
