$DATUM 8-(3-Chloro-5-(1-methyl-1H-indazol-5-yl)pyridin-4-yl)-2,8-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-1-one
(77) 8-(3-Bromo-5-chloropyridin-4-yl)-2,8-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-1-one 57
(250 mg, 0.725 mmol), 1- methyl-1H-indazol-5-ylboronic acid (153 mg,
0.870 mmol) and Pd(dppf)Cl2.CH2Cl2 (26.5 mg, 0.0360 mmol) were loaded in
a microwave vial under argon and then MeCN (13 mL) and 0.5 M aqueous
sodium carbonate solution (2.0 mL) were added. The reaction mixture was
heated at 120 °C for 60 min under microwave irradiation and then
concentrated. The crude material was purified via Biotage column
chromatography (CH2Cl2/EtOH 98/2 to 90/10). The title compound 77 (276
mg, 96% yield) as a white solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.29-1.35 (m,
2H), 1.89-1.96 (m, 4H), 2.67-2.75 (m, 2H), 3.12-3.18 (m, 2H), 3.25 (t, J
= 6.9 Hz, 2H), 4.13 (s, 3H), 5.71 (bs, 1H), 7.32 (dd, J = 8.6, 1.5 Hz,
1H), 7.49 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H), 7.64 (s, 1H), 8.04 (d, J = 0.9 Hz, 1H),
8.24 (s, 1H), 8.45 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 31.7, 32.3, 35.8,
38.5, 41.5, 47.6, 109.0, 121.1, 124.2, 128.2, 130.1, 133.0, 134.1, 139.3,
149.5, 151.1, 153.1, 181.3 (1 Cq not observed); LC (Method C) - MS (ESI,
m/z) Rt = 2.11 min – 396/398 (M+H)+. ESIHRMS: Found: 396.1583 calculated
for C21H23 35ClN5O (M+H)+: 396.1586.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, microwave irradiation, thermal, microwave vial used,
Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Potent, Orally Bioavailable, Small-Molecule Inhibitors of
WNT Signaling from a Cell-Based Pathway Screen
